{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AmtgYSKcddj6ZrEGqGfAb6","type":"tool_result","content":"-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent   6497 2026-10-28 21:50:04.981177050 +0000 claims_grounding.json\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent 280246 2026-10-28 21:56:10.977810474 +0000 paper.pdf\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent  44161 2026-10-28 21:55:32.257669011 +0000 paper.tex\n-rw------- 1 agent agent   5903 2026-10-28 21:57:23.396056069 +0000 paper_evidence_audit_feedback.json\n-rw------- 1 agent agent   7613 2026-10-28 21:44:55.361546384 +0000 references.bib\n-rw------- 1 agent agent   8289 2026-10-28 21:57:23.478199637 +0000 validation_feedback.json\n# Agentic evidence audit feedback\n\n- generated_at: `2026-10-28T21:57:23.395546+00:00`\n- ok: `False`\n- verdict: `fail`\n- finding_count: `4`\n- audit_json_path: `work/results/t06/claude/20261028_204856/paper/paper_evidence_audit.json`\n- audit_markdown_path: `work/results/t06/claude/20261028_204856/paper/paper_evidence_audit.md`\n- raw_output_path: `work/results/t06/claude/20261028_204856/paper/paper_evidence_audit_raw.txt`\n\n## Summary\nAll reported metrics, the qualification status and the attempt counts match paper_data.json and the evaluator source. Several descriptive claims go beyond the recorded evidence, though: related-work content, the search-scope context, and one implementation statement in the LLM-usage appendix.\n\n## Findings\n- `relwork-beyond-title-1` (Related Work / Introduction): The recorded provenance for these references holds only title, year and URL, with no abstract or text. The wording asserts specific content that no artifact supports. The paper discloses title-only knowledge for Seetharaman2021 and Yang2026 but not for these works.\n  - claim: Singh2025Illusion analyse \"private testing an52:Second, crowd-sourced leaderboards can be influenced deliberately, for instance through vote rigging \\citep{Min2025Rigging} or through differences in data access and sampling between providers \\citep{Singh2025Illusion}.\n58:The edits themselves are proposed by a one-shot first-order influence search in the spirit of influence functions \\citep{Koh2017Understanding} and approximate-robustness analysis of ``dropping a little data'' \\citep{Broderick2020Automatic}.\n82:The BT model \\citep{Bradley1952Rank} assigns each competitor a latent score and models the win probability of a pair as a logistic function of the score difference. Extensions handle ties \\citep{Davidson1970OnET}, order effects \\citep{Davidson1977OnET}, covariates \\citep{Yan2025InferenceIA}, temporal drift \\citep{Tian2023ASA}, continuous outcomes \\citep{Stern2011ModeratedPC,Fageot2023Generalize\n88:Influence functions estimate the effect of removing or perturbing a training point without refitting \\citep{Koh2017Understanding}. \\citet{Broderick2020Automatic} propose a finite-sample robustness metric asking whether dropping a small fraction of the data can change a conclusion, and use first-order influence approximations to find the data to drop. Our search is of this family, specialised to\n94:\\citet{Chiang2024Chatbot} describe the Chatbot Arena platform, in which users vote between two anonymous model responses and the votes are aggregated into rankings. \\citet{Min2025Rigging} study strategies by which votes on such platforms can be manipulated to change rankings, and \\citet{Singh2025Illusion} analyse evaluation practices on the same platform, including private testing and differenc\n125:\\emph{(i) Additivity.} The per-row effects are summed without modelling how $p_i$ and $A$ change after many rows are edited, so the heuristic can be inaccurate at a 2\\% budget even when it is accurate for one row; the accuracy of the underlying linear approximation is problem dependent \\citep{Giordano2018Swiss}, and we did not evaluate it for these data.\n313:The configuration studied here was chosen on a separate search data collection, on which it obtained a search-scope score of $0.914$ with a score delta of $0.0$ relative to the baseline (which is the selected configuration); the study outcome is recorded as completed without a qualifying winner and the selection kind is the baseline. % @evidence[[paper_data.json#downstream_study.baseline_score\n315:Unscored variants are missing performance evidence, not measured losses, and no comparison involving them appears anywhere in this paper. The search-scope score $0.914$ and the final score $0.606$ come from different data collections and scopes, with different designs (the search collection has no expert-human or LLM-judge data); they must not be read as a decline or a generalisation gap.\n319:Large language models were used throughout this work. An LLM-based research agent designed the three alternative search variants described above and wrote their code, none of which was scored; the studied search is the task's starter code. An LLM agent retrieved references through a literature-search API, planned the paper, wrote this manuscript and its claim-to-evidence mapping from the recor","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"84f4710a-b57d-47ca-82ad-cb6cbbf8aa55","uuid":"2bfe4c3e-f741-4f81-97ef-5fc61f21a369","timestamp":"2026-10-28T21:57:30.152Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent   6497 2026-10-28 21:50:04.981177050 +0000 claims_grounding.json\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent 280246 2026-10-28 21:56:10.977810474 +0000 paper.pdf\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent  44161 2026-10-28 21:55:32.257669011 +0000 paper.tex\n-rw------- 1 agent agent   5903 2026-10-28 21:57:23.396056069 +0000 paper_evidence_audit_feedback.json\n-rw------- 1 agent agent   7613 2026-10-28 21:44:55.361546384 +0000 references.bib\n-rw------- 1 agent agent   8289 2026-10-28 21:57:23.478199637 +0000 validation_feedback.json\n# Agentic evidence audit feedback\n\n- generated_at: `2026-10-28T21:57:23.395546+00:00`\n- ok: `False`\n- verdict: `fail`\n- finding_count: `4`\n- audit_json_path: `work/results/t06/claude/20261028_204