nformat\n241:\\paragraph{Design confounds and few cases.} The four designs are specific datasets, not random draws from design classes; they are confounded with size, number of competitors, margin and tie rate. Three of the four designs have one case per edit mode. The NBA data are game results, not preferenc\n315:Unscored variants are missing performance evidence, not measured losses, and no comparison involving them appears anywhere in this paper. The search-scope score $0.914$ and the final score $0.606$ come from different data collections and scopes, with different designs (the search collection has","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"84f4710a-b57d-47ca-82ad-cb6cbbf8aa55","uuid":"d44d863e-bbfb-4c0e-9d5d-1924a812d763","timestamp":"2026-10-28T21:57:41.751Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"1:@Article{Davidson1970OnET,\t5: title = {On Extending the Bradley-Terry Model to Accommodate Ties in Paired Comparison Experiments},\n10:@Article{Simons1999AsymptoticsWT,\t14: title = {Asymptotics when the number of parameters tends to infinity in the Bradley-Terry model for paired comparisons},\n19:@Article{Davidson1977OnET,\t23: title = {On Extending the Bradley-Terry Model to Incorporate Within-Pair Order Effects},\n28:@Article{Gao2021UncertaintyQI,\t30: booktitle = {Information and Inference A Journal of the IMA},\n32: title = {Uncertainty quantification in the Bradley–Terry–Luce model},\t36:@Article{Leonard1977AnAB,\n40: title = {An Alternative Bayesian Approach to the Bradley-Terry Model for Paired Comparisons},\t45:@Inproceedings{Bong2021GeneralizedRF,\n47: booktitle = {International Conference on Machine Learning},\t49: title = {Generalized Results for the Existence and Consistency of the MLE in the Bradley-Terry-Luce Model},\n53:@Article{Stern2011ModeratedPC,\t56: title = {Moderated paired comparisons: a generalized Bradley–Terry model for continuous data using a discontinuous penalized likelihood function},\n61:@Inproceedings{Fageot2023Generalize