{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01X3y5qKoSuYPNtDTxNptuhj","type":"tool_result","content":"158:The proposer is evaluated once on the sealed final data with three evaluation seeds (201, 202, 203). A seed only resets proposer state; it never selects data or workload. Because the proposer is deterministic, the three seeds are replicate executions of the same computation and carry no information about sampling variability of the data. Search-time scores were obtained on a separate proxy data collection (different Arena partition and NBA seasons, and no expert-human or LLM-judge data) and are reported only as separate context in Appendix~\\ref{app:selection}; they are never compared with the final scores.\n313:The configuration studied here was chosen on a separate search data collection, on which it obtained a search-scope score of $0.914$ with a score delta of $0.0$ relative to the baseline (which is the selected configuration); the study outcome is recorded as completed without a qualifying winner and the selection kind is the baseline. % @evidence[[paper_data.json#downstream_study.baseline_score]] @evidence[[paper_data.json#downstream_study.investigation_outcome]]\n315:Unscored variants are missing performance evidence, not measured losses, and no comparison involving them appears anywhere in this paper. The search-scope score $0.914$ and the final score $0.606$ come from different data collections and scopes, with different designs (the search collection has no expert-human or LLM-judge data); they must not be read as a decline or a generalisation gap.\n  \\edef\\watermarkScale{\\fpeval{0.8 * sqrt(\\paperwidth**2 + \\paperheight**2) / \\watermarkTextWidth}}%\n  \\edef\\watermarkAngle{\\fpeval{atand(\\paperheight/\\paperwidth)}}%\n  \\SetWatermarkScale{\\watermarkScale}%\n  \\SetWatermarkAngle{\\watermarkAngle}%\n}\n% --- end watermark ---\n % For LaTeX2e\n\\usepackage{paper,times}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"84f4710a-b57d-47ca-82ad-cb6cbbf8aa55","uuid":"bd1eb84c-cd9b-49b4-b9f9-dc1ca7039a42","timestamp":"2026-10-28T21:57:43.720Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"158:The proposer is evaluated once on the sealed final data with three evaluation seeds (201, 202, 203). A seed only resets proposer state; it never selects data or workload. Because the proposer is deterministic, the three seeds are replicate executions of the same computation and carry no information about sampling variability of the data. Search-time scores were obtained on a separate proxy data collection (different Arena partition and NBA seasons, and no expert-human or LLM-judge data) and are reported only as separate context in Appendix~\\ref{app:selection}; they are never compared with the final scores.\n313:The configuration studied here was chosen on a separate search data collection, on which it obtained a search-scope score of $0.914$ with a score delta of $0.0$ relative to the baseline (which is the selected configuration); the study outcome is recorded as completed without a qualifying winner and the selection kind is the baseline. % @evidence[[paper_data.json#downstream_study.baseline_score]] @evidence[[paper_data.json#downstream_study.investigation_outcome]]\n315:Unscored variants are missing performance evidence, not measured losses, and no comparison involving them appears anywhere in this paper. The search-scope score $0.914$ and the final score $0.606$ come from different data collections and scopes, with different designs (the search collection has no expert-human or LLM-judge data); they must not be read as a decline or a generalisation gap.\n  \\edef\\watermarkScale{\\fpeval{0.8 * sqrt(\\paperwidth**2 + \\paperheight**2) / \\watermarkTextWidth}}%\n  \\edef\\watermarkAngle{\\fpeval{atand(\\paperheight/\\paperwidth)}}%\n  \\SetWatermarkScale{\\watermarkScale}%\n  \\SetWatermarkAngle{\\watermarkAngle}%\n}\n% --- end watermark ---\n % For LaTeX2e\n\\usepackage{paper,times}","stderr":